# DealAtlas Agent Rules

Before making changes, inspect the current implementation and adapt to what already exists. Do not assume the repository is in the state described by the master specification.

Read relevant `/docs` files before implementing a feature.

## Product priority
The anti-bypass rule is non-negotiable:
- free/anonymous clients must not receive buyer identity, source identity, exact source title, source URL, notice/reference identifiers, original documents, procurement contacts, or combinations of exact facts that make reverse lookup trivial;
- do not hide protected data with CSS or client rendering;
- protected data must not be sent to the client before paid entitlement is verified server-side.

## Database/security
- Do not disable RLS to fix a bug.
- Do not broaden anon/authenticated grants casually.
- Do not expose Supabase secret/service keys.
- Do not use client-side plan/role values as authorization.
- Canonical source-bearing tables remain server-only.
- Public/free search must use `deal_previews` only.
- Subscriber detail routes must verify auth + entitlement before trusted query.
- Admin mutations must verify admin role server-side.
- Migrations are append-only after they have been applied to production.

## Billing
- Dodo checkout redirect is not proof of entitlement.
- Only verified webhook/provider reconciliation grants Pro.
- Webhook handling must be idempotent.
- Product IDs are allowlisted server-side and loaded from environment.
- Never trust a product ID/plan/user ID supplied by browser without validation.

## Ingestion
- Prefer official APIs/open data.
- Do not bypass CAPTCHAs, logins, access controls or anti-bot restrictions.
- Do not automate a source with UNKNOWN or PROHIBITED reuse status.
- Preserve raw provenance and source versions.
- Source adapters must fail independently.
- Never silently discard malformed records.

## Quality
For every goal:
1. inspect existing code;
2. make the smallest coherent changes that satisfy the specification;
3. reuse existing patterns/components;
4. avoid duplicate architectures;
5. validate input;
6. add/update tests;
7. run lint, typecheck/build and relevant tests;
8. fix failures caused by the work;
9. inspect final diff for unrelated changes;
10. update docs when architecture/behaviour changed.

Never claim completion while known critical/blocking tests fail.

## UI
Follow `/docs/DESIGN.md`.
Do not blur protected source text that has already been sent to the browser.
Do not invent statistics, live opportunity counts or customer claims.

## Scope
Do not add CRM, bid-writing AI, team workspaces, public API, mobile apps or unrelated enterprise features before the launch requirements in `/docs/PRODUCT.md` are complete.
